description:
Implement an 8-bit barrel shifter that processes an input data byte based on a 3-bit shift control signal. Depending on the value of the shift signal, the module will shift the input data left by 0 to 7 bits, and the output will capture the bits from positions 7 to 5 of the resulting shifted data. This design is useful for operations requiring variable bit shifting, such as in digital signal processing or arithmetic operations.
module top_module(
    input [7:0] data_i,
    input [2:0] shift_i,
    output [2:0] data_o
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [7:0] data_i,
    input [2:0] shift_i,
    output [2:0] data_o
    );reg [15:0] tmp;
   always @*
      case (shift_i)
         3'b000: tmp = data_i;
         3'b001: tmp = data_i << 1;
         3'b010: tmp = data_i << 2;
         3'b011: tmp = data_i << 3;
         3'b100: tmp = data_i << 4;
         3'b101: tmp = data_i << 5;
         3'b110: tmp = data_i << 6;
         default: tmp = data_i << 7;
      endcase
	assign data_o = tmp[7:5];endmodule

