description:
Implement a 4-bit magnitude comparator that determines the relationship between two 4-bit inputs, A and B. The output, `result`, indicates whether A is greater than B by analyzing derived values from the sum and difference of A and B. Specifically, the comparator utilizes bitwise conditions to evaluate the sign bits and the two least significant bits of the sum to decide if A is greater than B, effectively providing a comparison result without generating direct equality or less-than outputs.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output result
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output result
);wire [3:0] sum;
    wire [3:0] diff;

    assign sum = A + ~B + 1;
    assign diff = A - B;

    assign result = (sum[3] & diff[3]) | (~diff[3] & sum[2]) | (~diff[3] & ~sum[3] & sum[1]) | (~diff[3] & ~sum[3] & ~sum[1] & sum[0]);

endmodule

