description:
Design a Power-on Reset (POR) circuit that generates a reset signal after a specified delay whenever the power-on reset input (por) is asserted. The circuit uses a counter driven by a 100 MHz clock to measure the delay duration. Upon receiving a rising edge on the por input, the counter resets and starts counting until it reaches a preset value corresponding to the defined delay (1 second). Once the count exceeds this delay, the reset output is asserted high, indicating that the system is ready to operate. The reset signal remains active until the next power-on reset event.
module top_module(
  input por,
  input clk,          // Added clk input
  output reg reset
);

code:
module top_module(
  input por,
  input clk,          // Added clk input
  output reg reset
);parameter delay = 1; // delay time in seconds

reg [31:0] count = 0;
reg delay_done = 0;

always @(posedge por) begin
  count <= 0;
  delay_done <= 0;
  reset <= 0;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (delay_done) begin
    reset <= 1;
    count <= 0;
  end else if (por) begin
    count <= count + 1;
    if (count >= delay * 100000000) begin // 100MHz clock assumed
      delay_done <= 1;
    end
  end
end

endmodule

