description:
Design a circuit that generates a pulse output every 250 negative edges of the input bclk signal. The output pulse is high for one clock cycle whenever the count of negative edges reaches 250. The module uses an 8-bit counter to keep track of the number of clock cycles, resetting once it reaches the threshold.
module top_module(
    input  bclk,
    output out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input  bclk,
    output out
);reg pulse;
reg [7:0] count = 0;

always @(negedge bclk)
    if (count >= 250) begin
        pulse = 1;
        count = 0;
    end
    else begin
        pulse = 0;
        count = count + 1;
    end

assign out = pulse;

endmodule

