description:
Design a circuit to calculate the even parity bit for an 8-bit input data. The module counts the number of set bits (1s) in the input and generates a parity_bit output: it outputs a HIGH (1) if the count of 1s is odd, indicating that the parity is odd, and LOW (0) if the count is even, indicating even parity.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] data,
  output reg parity_bit
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] data,
  output reg parity_bit
);integer i;
  reg [7:0] temp_data;
  reg [3:0] count;

  always @* begin
    temp_data = data;
    count = 0;
    for(i=0; i<8; i=i+1) begin
      count = count + temp_data[i];
    end
    if(count % 2 == 1) begin
      parity_bit = 1;
    end
    else begin
      parity_bit = 0;
    end
  end

endmodule

