Design a 4-bit wide combinational logic module named OR3 that performs specified bit-wise operations on two 4-bit inputs, A and B. For the least significant bit (Z[0]) and the most significant bit (Z[3]), the module outputs the logical OR of the corresponding bits from A and B. For the second bit (Z[1]), it also outputs the logical OR of A[1] and B[1]. However, for the middle bit (Z[2]), it outputs the logical XOR of A[2] and B[2]. This configuration allows for selective bit-wise logical operations based on the input signals.
