description:
Design a circuit that checks for errors in a 4-bit input value. If the input \( n \) exceeds the binary value 1100 (decimal 12), the circuit signals an error by setting the output \( error \) to 1 and outputs a corrected value of 0. If the input is within the valid range, \( error \) is set to 0, and the output \( correct \) will mirror the input \( n \).
module top_module(

    input wire [3:0] n,
    output reg [3:0] correct,
    output reg error
    );

code:
module top_module(

    input wire [3:0] n,
    output reg [3:0] correct,
    output reg error
    );always@(n)
        begin
            if(n > 4'b1100)
                begin
                    error <= 1;
                    correct <= 0;
                end
            else
                begin
                    error <= 0;
                    correct <= n;
                end
        end       
endmodule

